{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Connect ChatGPT — UCESCO Volunteer Manager{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6">
        <a href="{{ path('connect_ai_index') }}" class="inline-block text-sm text-slate-600 hover:underline">← Connect an AI Agent</a>

        <div>
            <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold">Connect ChatGPT</h1>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
                Takes about three minutes, in ChatGPT in a browser. You won't need a password or secret from anyone:
                you sign in with your own Mikono account.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5 text-sm text-amber-900" aria-labelledby="account-heading">
            <h2 id="account-heading" class="font-semibold">A Free or personal ChatGPT account has consumer terms</h2>
            <p class="mt-1">
                Volunteers' data will fall under the terms of the ChatGPT account you connect, and OpenAI receives it
                outside Kenya. Use a UCESCO work account if there is one. On a Free or personal account, before
                anything else open <a href="https://chatgpt.com/settings/data-controls" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-medium underline">Data controls</a>
                in ChatGPT's settings and turn off <strong>Improve the model for everyone</strong>. It's on by default,
                and while it's on, what ChatGPT reads from Mikono may be used for training.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm" aria-labelledby="values-heading">
            <h2 id="values-heading" class="font-semibold">The two things to paste</h2>
            {{ include('connect_ai/_copy_field.html.twig', {id: 'mcp-url', label: 'Server URL', value: mcpUrl}) }}
            {{ include('connect_ai/_copy_field.html.twig', {id: 'client-id', label: 'OAuth client ID', value: clientId}) }}
        </section>

        <section class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm" aria-labelledby="steps-heading">
            <h2 id="steps-heading" class="font-semibold">Steps</h2>
            <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-slate-700">
                <li>Open <a href="https://chatgpt.com/plugins" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">chatgpt.com/plugins</a>, click <strong>Add</strong> at the top right, and choose <strong>Add custom MCP server</strong>.</li>
                <li>Name it <strong>Mikono</strong>, leave the description and icon empty, keep <strong>Server URL</strong> selected, and paste the <strong>Server URL</strong>.</li>
                <li>Keep <strong>Authentication</strong> on <strong>OAuth</strong>. Wait a few seconds: <strong>Advanced OAuth settings</strong> stays greyed out until ChatGPT has read the URL. Then open it. A second panel appears beside the form.</li>
                <li>Check that <strong>Registration method</strong> says <strong>User-Defined OAuth Client</strong>, and paste the <strong>OAuth client ID</strong>. The red notes saying DCR and CIMD are unavailable are expected.</li>
                <li><strong>Leave the client secret empty</strong>, keep <strong>Token endpoint auth method</strong> on <strong>none</strong>, and keep the <strong>read</strong> scope ticked. Scroll down inside the panel to see them.</li>
                <li>Scroll down the form on the left, tick <strong>I understand and want to continue</strong>, and click <strong>Create as a plugin</strong>. This takes about ten seconds.</li>
                <li>When ChatGPT asks, click <strong>Connect Mikono</strong>.</li>
                <li>Mikono opens. Sign in if asked, read the screen, and click <strong>Allow</strong>. You land back in ChatGPT.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
                <strong>Check it worked:</strong> the
                <a href="{{ path('connect_ai_index') }}" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">Connect an AI Agent</a>
                page should say your account is connected.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
                <strong>If Mikono didn't open:</strong> the first <strong>Connect Mikono</strong> click can close the
                dialog without going anywhere, even though the plugin was created. Don't add the server again. On
                chatgpt.com/plugins, click the new icon under <strong>Installed</strong>, click <strong>Connect</strong>
                next to Mikono, then <strong>Connect Mikono</strong> again.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm" aria-labelledby="try-heading">
            <h2 id="try-heading" class="font-semibold">Try it</h2>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
                On the Mikono plugin page, click <strong>Try in chat</strong>, then ask:
                <em>"How many volunteers are present right now, and at which branches?"</em>
                Check an answer by following its links back to Mikono: ChatGPT can be wrong. Your reads then appear on
                the <a href="{{ path('usage_index') }}" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">Usage</a> page.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
                Mikono doesn't record hours, children supported, contact history or deadlines. If ChatGPT gives a figure
                for one of those, treat it as a guess.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm" aria-labelledby="stop-heading">
            <h2 id="stop-heading" class="font-semibold">To stop</h2>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
                Click <strong>Disconnect</strong> on the <a href="{{ path('connect_ai_index') }}" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">Connect an AI Agent</a>
                page. It ends every assistant connected to your account, so reconnect any you still want. Do this
                straight away if you lose a device signed in to ChatGPT. Losing the admin role, or having your account
                deactivated, cuts the connection too.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
